diff -ruN original/LL_MIGRATION.md updated/LL_MIGRATION.md
--- original/LL_MIGRATION.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ updated/LL_MIGRATION.md	2026-11-13 17:25:27.739857852 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# STM32 LL migration notes
+
+## Setup
+
+Place the **STM32CubeH7** firmware distribution at `vendor/STM32CubeH7/`.
+The CMake project includes `Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Inc` and uses
+header-only LL operations. Keep the existing ARM CMSIS and STM32H7 device
+headers/submodules; do **not** include a second copy of the CMSIS device headers.
+The package version must match STM32H743 and its CMSIS device definitions.
+No CubeIDE or CubeMX initialization code is used.
+
+## Responsibilities
+
+- `platform/`: Core/CMSIS SysTick, fault capture, MPU, SWO and TinyUSB retained.
+  GPIO and SPI/I2C peripheral setup now use LL where appropriate; polling
+  transaction state machines remain locally implemented for now.
+- `board/`: Pin configuration, RF power enable, battery CE/status and bus configs.
+- `drivers/`: AD4683 protocol, BQ25883 register operations, ADF4158 serial protocol.
+- `src/system/io.c`: Lightweight printf routing; select SWO or USB for diagnostics.
+
+The driver API and existing AD4683 paired-polling transfer remain functional in
+concept; the latter still needs revalidation on hardware after modifying SPI setup.
+
+## Important validation
+
+1. Confirm GPIO and LL SPI configuration produces the same electrical signals.
+2. Confirm SPI4 hardware NSS and SPI5 master mode still receive both ADC words.
+3. Confirm BQ25883 CE stays HIGH at reset and charger remains disabled; any
+   later charge enable must be deliberate.
+4. Confirm the RF board powers from **both** RF 5 V and RF 15 V rails before ADC tests.
+5. Confirm 25 MHz HSE and PLL USB clock assumptions against the PCB.
+6. Confirm I2C4 timing values against the selected kernel clock and rise times.
+7. Confirm non-cacheable MPU region and linker DMA-buffer placement before
+   implementing ADC DMA. Do not use polling-based paired transfers for final capture.
+
+## SDMMC/HAL later
+
+Add `stm32h7xx_hal_conf.h` to `include/`, enable only the HAL modules needed by
+SDMMC, include `stm32h7xx_hal.c` plus SDMMC and DMA support sources, and provide
+`HAL_GetTick()`/MSP callbacks through a dedicated platform adapter. Keep HAL
+exclusive to the SDMMC peripheral and expose a platform-owned block-device API
+above it. FatFs goes above that API. Do not enable HAL source files now.
+
+## Known outstanding limitations
+
+- This zip omits the original `vendor/` contents; full firmware build is not
+  possible until the user installs dependencies.
+- The SPI5/SPI4 capture remains **polling**, without timer-triggered DMA.
+- `ad4683_init()` writes CONFIGURATION1 = 0x002 to select external 3.3 V
+  REFIO using the existing 0x9002 command. Verify this with ADC input test;
+  full register readback is not yet implemented.
+- The 480 MHz clock tree, USB clock, fixed I2C timing value and MPU setup retain
+  the existing hardware-proven configuration; migrate them separately only if
+  measurements show a need.
